    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 0.96,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.04,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings plateau at about 0.96 from 6 h onward, which could have been detector saturation. I diluted the 18 h aliquot to check. A 10-fold dilution read 0.0953 (0.094 and 0.0967), which scales to 0.953. A 3-fold dilution read 0.3265 (0.3127 and 0.3402), which scales to 0.98. Both match the undiluted reading of 0.9625 within replicate noise, so the reader is responding proportionally at this density. If it were saturating, the diluted samples would scale to well above 0.96. The plateau is therefore real stationary phase, and the biomass is at the level the undiluted readings indicate."
  },
